Thank you for the compliment, but I'd think that "Pacifist" would be
harder because a single accidental bump-kill and the conduct is down
the drain.  But for this project, the extra kills just tally.  Based
on my experience, a player with patience and focus could probably get
their kill list below 200 and probably even below 100.  The other big
help would have been writing or finding a spellbook of sleep.  With
the Eye, sleep could have been heavily spammed, thereby keeping much
of the dungeon's denizens safe from themselves (in hindsight).

Also, I should have had a better plan for the Gnomish Mines as so many
gnomes died there.  Again, sleep would have helped but finding some
way to keep them from shooting each other with arrows and daggers is
key.  It looks like G's accounted for 29 kills (over 10%) despite not
using them for experience.

Here is my list and some additional comments.  Of the advanced
monsters I count 25, at least, that didn't need to die.  Excepting
gnomes, bump kills and experience fodder comprises much of the
remaining 200.  I'm also interested in just how low a vanquish list
could go.  Incidentally, I did not come across any bones files.
Acquiring Magicbane is kind of a benchmark as it allows one to make
far better time through the dungeon.  But, of course, getting
Magicbane requires creature sacrifice.

Sokoban, I found, required, for the most part, killing creatures.  At
first I tried to just dust Elbereth, or to zap sleep (when I had the
spell in other attempts) but the number of creatures just keeps
building up the longer you spend there.

